<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33575" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλελίζω</span></b>  (B), aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠλέλιξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.2.14
				</span></i>
			, 
				Ep.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Del.</u>
					137
				</span></i>
			:— <i>cry</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλελεῦ</span>, hence, <i>raise the
				battle-cry</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ Ἐνυαλίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					1.8.18
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>raise a loud cry</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1514
			</span></i> (lyr.); of a shield, <i>ring</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
			</span></i> l.c.:—
				Med.
			, of the nightingale, <i>trill her lay of sorrow</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1111
			</span></i> (lyr.): c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴτυν ἐλελιζομένη</span>
			<i>trilling her lament for</i> Itys, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				213
			</span></i> (lyr., but punctuation is dub.).</div>
